<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="claims-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="claims-title">Schemes and defective-part claims</h2>
      <p>Brand schemes often reach you as credit notes or free goods, long after the sale. If you only record them on arrival, monthly margin swings for no real reason, and unclaimed amounts can quietly lapse.</p>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>Keep a list of open claims, with the date each was sent</li>
        <li>Mark defective pieces apart from saleable stock</li>
        <li>Record a replacement against the original claim</li>
        <li>Ask how free goods and post-sale discounts affect GST and stock value</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Part numbers and fitment</h2>
      <p>The same part may come from several brands, and may also be sold under another code. If your billing software lists one part twice, stock will be wrong even when each bill is right.</p>
      <p class="para">Agree one naming rule and clean the master list before moving to new software. See {% routeLink "/services/tally-zoho-accounting/", "Tally and Zoho accounting" %}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="used-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="used-title">Selling to workshops and mechanics</h2>
      <p>Many mechanics buy small amounts, on running credit, and may not be registered. Issue a bill for each sale, and enter each part payment against the correct party. Rule 46 of the CGST Rules requires an unregistered buyer's name and address on the invoice where the taxable value is ₹50,000 or more.</p>
      <p class="para">If you also fit parts, as well as sell them, ask how a bill with both goods and labour should be treated.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Used parts, and goods going out of Delhi</h2>
      <p>If you deal in used parts without taking input tax credit, ask whether the margin-based value in rule 32(5) applies. Keep each purchase record, since the rule depends on it.</p>
      <p class="para">For deliveries, rule 138 asks a registered person moving a consignment worth more than ₹50,000 to furnish e-way bill details before it moves. Combined orders can cross that figure quickly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="area-title">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2 id="area-title" class="first-h2">About the area, and about us</h2>
    <p>Trade guides describe Kashmere Gate as a major wholesale market for automobile parts, serving retailers, mechanics and workshops, with nearby Mori Gate known for commercial vehicle parts. Claims about its size come from guides and promotional pages, so we do not repeat them.</p>
    <p>AccountOrbit has no office here, and takes enquiries by phone from anywhere in Delhi. If you are thinking of moving to new billing software, mention it on the first call, since the part master list is best cleaned before the move.</p>
  </div>
</section>

